# AI Testing Strategy

## Prompt Testing
- Develop a unit test suite for prompts
- Test edge cases and unusual inputs
- Verify prompt robustness against different models
- Evaluate prompt performance using automated tests
- Build a prompt regression test library
- Verify prompt improvements using control group tests
- Test prompts of varying length and complexity
- Implement parameterized testing for prompt templates

## Agent Behavior Testing
- Define expected agent behavior and outcomes
- Develop test scenarios that simulate different user interactions
- Test the agent's decision-making capabilities under various conditions
- Use continuous integration to run tests automatically
- Build an agent behavior simulation environment
- Test correctness and efficiency of task completion
- Evaluate the agent's ability to handle ambiguous or incomplete instructions
- Test agent memory and context tracking capabilities

## Integration Testing
- Test the integration of the agent with external systems and tools
- Verify data flows and interactions
- Test dependencies using mock services
- Monitor performance and resource utilization
- Test the system's behavior under different load conditions
- Verify error handling and failure recovery mechanisms
- Test API limits and quota management
- Evaluate the impact of network and service outages

## Security Testing
- Develop tests for prompt injections
- Test model jailbreak attempts
- Test permission boundaries and data access restrictions
- Conduct regular security audits
- Implement vulnerability scans and penetration tests
- Test compliance with sensitive data handling
- Verify authentication and authorization mechanisms
- Evaluate logging and audit trail capabilities

## User Experience Testing
- Evaluate the quality and relevance of agent responses
- Measure response times and user waiting experience
- Collect user feedback and satisfaction metrics
- Conduct A/B testing to compare different agent versions
- Evaluate the naturalness and coherence of the agent's language
- Test adaptability to different user skill levels
- Evaluate the reliability of the agent in critical tasks
- Test the performance of the agent on various devices and interfaces

## Performance Testing
- Measure response times and latency
- Evaluate concurrent request handling capabilities
- Monitor resource usage (memory, CPU, GPU)
- Conduct load and stress testing
- Evaluate scalability and capacity planning
- Test long-running stability
- Identify performance bottlenecks and optimization opportunities
- Evaluate the cost-benefit ratio of different configurations

## Test automation and continuous testing
- Establish an automated test pipeline
- Implement a continuous testing process
- Use a test-driven development (TDD) approach
- Establish test coverage goals and monitoring
- Implement a regression testing strategy
- Automate test result analysis and reporting
- Integrate testing into CI/CD workflows
- Use chaos engineering to test system resilience